{"name":"Sorcerer","hex":"#3398ce","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sorcerer","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A magician or wizard. Sometimes specifically male.","A person whose skills or abilities appear almost magical."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sorcerer"}],"entries":[{"title":"Magic (supernatural)","blocks":[{"text":"Magic, sometimes spelled magick, is the application of beliefs, rituals or actions employed with the intent to manipulate natural or supernatural beings and forces. It is a category into which various beliefs and practices have been placed, sometimes considered separate from both religion and science. This separation of the terms 'religion' and 'magic' in a functional sense is disputed. It is a postulate of modern anthropology, at least since early 1930s, that there is complete continuity between magic and religion."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/RWS_Tarot_01_Magician.jpg/330px-RWS_Tarot_01_Magician.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magic_(supernatural)"},{"title":"Magician (fantasy)","blocks":[{"text":"A magician, also known as a mage, magus, magic-user, spellcaster, enchanter/enchantress, sorcerer/sorceress, warlock, witch, or wizard, is someone who uses or practices magic derived from supernatural, occult, or arcane sources. Magicians enjoy a rich history in mythology, legends, fiction, and folklore, and are common figures in works of fantasy, such as fantasy literature and role-playing games."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/The_Enchanted_Garden_of_Messer_Ansaldo_by_Marie_Spartali_Stillman_%281889%29.jpg/330px-The_Enchanted_Garden_of_Messer_Ansaldo_by_Marie_Spartali_Stillman_%281889%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magician_(fantasy)"},{"title":"Sorcerer (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Sorcerer is a 1977 American action thriller film produced and directed by William Friedkin and starring Roy Scheider, Bruno Cremer, Francisco Rabal, and Amidou. It is the second adaptation of Georges Arnaud's 1950 novel The Wages of Fear, following the 1953 French-language film. Although it is often considered a remake of the earlier film, Friedkin disagreed with this assessment, considering it another adaptation of the novel with an entirely different vision."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a7/Sorcerer77poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sorcerer_(film)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Heptameron_magic_circle.jpg/500px-Heptameron_magic_circle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Heptameron_magic_circle.jpg/500px-Heptameron_magic_circle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHeptameron_magic_circle.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Herodotos_Met_91.8.jpg/500px-Herodotos_Met_91.8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Herodotos_Met_91.8.jpg/1280px-Herodotos_Met_91.8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Herodotos_Met_91.8.jpg/500px-Herodotos_Met_91.8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"One of the earliest surviving accounts of the Persian mágoi was provided by the Greek historian Herodotus.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHerodotos_Met_91.8.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/common